      "extract": "Define the `center' $Z_0(X)$ of a set $X$ to be the monoid of all functions $f\\colon X\\rightarrow X$ (with composition as product and the identity map as unit.) Then the usual center $Z_1\\equiv Z$ of the monoid $Z_0(X)$ is trivial: $Z_1(Z_0(X))=\\{\\id_X\\}$. The cardinality of $Z_0(X)$ is given by $\\#Z_0(X)=\\#X^{\\#X}$. The aim of the present work is to prove 1-categorical analogues of these trivial set theoretic (=",
